  "body": "Currently we store the latest transaction id for a `(path, access_token)` tuple. This is problematic in the case tjat a client sends, say, two messages at the same time _and the first to arrive at the server is retried_. This first txn id is inserted into the transaction store, and is then immediately clobbered by the second txn id.\n\nThis results in duplicates.\n\n(Imported from https://matrix.org/jira/browse/SYN-603)\n\n(Reported by @erikjohnston)",
